home='''<section class="ts-hero"><div class="ts-wrap ts-hero-grid"><div><p class="ts-eyebrow">For Electricians, Plumbers, Roofers, and General Contractors</p><h1>Turn more inquiries into booked work.</h1><p class="ts-hero-lede">Top Shelf connects visibility, response, follow-up, booking, estimate follow-up, and reviews into one system built for how established contractors actually run their day.</p><div class="ts-hero-actions"><a class="ts-btn ts-btn-solid" data-event="audit_cta_click" href="/growth-audit/">Get Your Opportunity Snapshot</a><a class="ts-hero-link" href="#opportunity-snapshot">See What We Review</a></div></div><aside class="ts-ticket"><p class="ts-ticket-time">Tuesday, 2:14 PM</p><h2>You&#8217;re mid-job. The next call still gets answered.</h2><p class="ts-ticket-flow">Missed call <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span> Text sent <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span> Job booked</p><p class="ts-ticket-note">An example of the process. Not a client result.</p></aside></div></section>

<section class="ts-audience ts-reveal"><div class="ts-wrap"><p class="ts-audience-label">Top Shelf works with established home-service businesses, including:</p><div class="ts-audience-grid"><div class="ts-audience-item"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M13 2 4 14h6l-1 8 9-12h-6l1-8Z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>Electricians</span></div><div class="ts-audience-item"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 3h8M9 3v4a3 3 0 0 0 6 0V3M12 10v11M8 21h8" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>Plumbers</span></div><div class="ts-audience-item"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 12 12 5l9 7M6 12v8h12v-8" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>Roofers</span></div><div class="ts-audience-item"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14.7 6.3a3 3 0 0 1 4 4L9 20l-5 1 1-5Z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>General Contractors</span></div></div></div></section>

<section class="ts-section ts-section-compact ts-reveal"><div class="ts-wrap ts-problem-grid"><div class="ts-head"><p class="ts-eyebrow">Where opportunity leaks</p><h2>Good work is not the problem. The gaps around it are.</h2><p class="ts-lede">Most lost jobs are not lost on quality. They slip away in the moments between an inquiry and a booked job, or between a finished job and the next one.</p></div><ol class="ts-ledger"><li class="ts-ledger-row"><span class="ts-ledger-num">01</span><div><h3>Inquiry to first response</h3><p>A homeowner reaches out. How long before someone actually replies?</p></div></li><li class="ts-ledger-row"><span class="ts-ledger-num">02</span><div><h3>Missed call to recovery</h3><p>The phone rings during a job. What happens next decides whether that lead is still warm.</p></div></li><li class="ts-ledger-row"><span class="ts-ledger-num">03</span><div><h3>Estimate to follow-up</h3><p>A quote goes out. Without a next step, it quietly goes cold.</p></div></li><li class="ts-ledger-row"><span class="ts-ledger-num">04</span><div><h3>Completed job to review</h3><p>The work is done and the customer is happy. Asking for a review is easy to forget.</p></div></li><li class="ts-ledger-row"><span class="ts-ledger-num">05</span><div><h3>One-time customer to repeat work</h3><p>A satisfied customer becomes a repeat customer only if someone stays in touch.</p></div></li></ol></div></section>

<section class="ts-section ts-reveal"><div class="ts-wrap"><div class="ts-head"><p class="ts-eyebrow">One connected system</p><h2>Four systems, working together.</h2><p class="ts-lede">Each piece hands off to the next, so nothing depends on someone remembering to follow up.</p></div><div class="ts-systems-grid"><article class="ts-system"><span class="ts-system-num">01</span><h3>Get Found</h3><p class="ts-system-sub">Visibility and reputation</p><p>Show up clearly online and keep new customers finding you.</p></article><article class="ts-system"><span class="ts-system-num">02</span><h3>Respond Fast</h3><p class="ts-system-sub">Lead capture, missed-call recovery, speed-to-lead</p><p>Capture the call, text, or form the moment it happens, even when you can&#8217;t pick up.</p></article><article class="ts-system"><span class="ts-system-num">03</span><h3>Turn Interest Into Booked Work</h3><p class="ts-system-sub">Automated follow-up, booking, estimate follow-up</p><p>Keep estimates and inquiries moving until they become a scheduled job.</p></article><article class="ts-system"><span class="ts-system-num">04</span><h3>Build Repeat Demand</h3><p class="ts-system-sub">Reviews, retention, customer experience</p><p>Turn finished jobs into honest reviews and repeat calls.</p></article></div></div></section>

<section class="ts-section ts-snapshot ts-reveal" id="opportunity-snapshot"><div class="ts-wrap ts-snapshot-grid"><div><p class="ts-eyebrow">The first step</p><h2>Get Your Opportunity Snapshot</h2><p class="ts-lede">This is the same practical review Top Shelf has always offered, now with a clearer name. It is a diagnostic first step, not a software signup.</p><ul class="ts-check-list"><li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>Missed calls and how fast you respond</li><li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>How inquiries and estimates are followed up</li><li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>How, and whether, you ask for reviews</li><li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>What is publicly visible about your business online</li><li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>Where the owner or office ends up doing repetitive manual work</li></ul><p class="ts-snapshot-note">We start with what is already working. Where we cannot confirm something publicly, we say so rather than assume it is missing. Any opportunity we surface still needs your confirmation.</p></div><div class="ts-snapshot-side"><h3>What you receive</h3><p>A short, honest look at up to three specific opportunities, focused on revenue, customer experience, and owner time, along with what is already working well. Stephen Wierzbicki reviews what you share, verifies what is publicly visible, and follows up directly.</p><a class="ts-btn ts-btn-solid" data-event="audit_cta_click" href="/growth-audit/">Get Your Opportunity Snapshot</a><p class="ts-snapshot-fine">Not a software trial. Not an automatic sign-up.</p></div></div></section>

<section class="ts-progression ts-reveal"><div class="ts-wrap"><div class="ts-progression-caption"><p class="ts-eyebrow">How a job moves through the system</p><h2>One inquiry, followed all the way through.</h2></div><ol class="ts-rail"><li><span class="ts-rail-label">Inquiry</span><span class="ts-rail-state">Received</span></li><li><span class="ts-rail-label">Responded</span><span class="ts-rail-state">Same day</span></li><li><span class="ts-rail-label">Booked</span><span class="ts-rail-state">Scheduled</span></li><li><span class="ts-rail-label">Estimate</span><span class="ts-rail-state">Followed up</span></li><li><span class="ts-rail-label">Job</span><span class="ts-rail-state">Completed</span></li><li><span class="ts-rail-label">Review</span><span class="ts-rail-state">Requested</span></li><li><span class="ts-rail-label">Referral</span><span class="ts-rail-state">Repeat work</span></li></ol><p class="ts-progression-note">An illustration of the process. Actual steps depend on what your business already has in place.</p></div></section>

<section class="ts-section ts-section-compact ts-reveal"><div class="ts-wrap"><div class="ts-head"><p class="ts-eyebrow">How we work</p><h2>A practical method, not a guess.</h2></div><div class="ts-method"><div class="ts-method-row"><h3>What we inspect</h3><p>We start with what is publicly visible: response speed signals, review activity, and basic online visibility. Nothing about your internal systems is assumed.</p></div><div class="ts-method-row"><h3>How we prioritize</h3><p>Opportunities are ranked by likely effect on revenue, customer experience, and owner time, not by what is easiest to sell.</p></div><div class="ts-method-row"><h3>What implementation can include</h3><p>Depending on what is confirmed, work may include missed-call recovery, follow-up sequences, booking, review requests, and reporting, connected as one system rather than separate tools.</p></div><div class="ts-method-row"><h3>How the journey stays connected</h3><p>Every piece is built to hand off cleanly to the next: a missed call becomes a text, a completed job becomes a review request, without extra manual steps.</p></div><div class="ts-method-row"><h3>What you receive</h3><p>A clear explanation of what was found, what it could mean for your business, and what testing looks like before anything goes live.</p></div></div></div></section>

<section class="ts-section ts-reveal"><div class="ts-wrap"><div class="ts-head"><p class="ts-eyebrow">Why Top Shelf</p><h2>Built around how contractors actually work.</h2></div><div class="ts-why-grid"><article class="ts-why-item"><h3>Contractor-context first</h3><p>We understand how estimates, callbacks, and job scheduling actually work in the field.</p></article><article class="ts-why-item"><h3>One connected customer journey</h3><p>Visibility, response, follow-up, booking, and reviews work together instead of living in separate tools.</p></article><article class="ts-why-item"><h3>Fast-response systems</h3><p>The moments right after an inquiry or missed call matter most, and they are built to move fast.</p></article><article class="ts-why-item"><h3>Practical follow-up</h3><p>Estimates and inquiries get a real next step instead of going quiet.</p></article><article class="ts-why-item"><h3>Reputation after the job</h3><p>Honest review requests go out after work is actually completed.</p></article><article class="ts-why-item"><h3>Built around owner time</h3><p>Every system is built to reduce repetitive work for the owner or office, not add to it.</p></article></div></div></section>

<section class="ts-section ts-section-compact ts-reveal"><div class="ts-wrap"><div class="ts-head"><p class="ts-eyebrow">Questions</p><h2>Straight answers before you request a Snapshot.</h2></div><div class="ts-faq-list"><details><summary><h3>Is this another lead-generation package?</h3></summary><p>No. Top Shelf focuses on what happens after someone reaches out, not on generating more traffic. The goal is to help you keep and convert the inquiries you are already getting.</p></details><details><summary><h3>Do I need to replace my current tools?</h3></summary><p>Not without a verified reason and your approval. We start by confirming what is already working and build around it where we can.</p></details><details><summary><h3>What does the Opportunity Snapshot include?</h3></summary><p>A short review of your visibility, response speed, follow-up, and review activity, focused on up to three specific opportunities along with what is already working well.</p></details><details><summary><h3>What happens after the Snapshot?</h3></summary><p>You will hear directly from Top Shelf with what was found. Nothing is recommended or built before it is confirmed with you.</p></details><details><summary><h3>Is this only for large contractors?</h3></summary><p>No. It is built for established electricians, plumbers, roofers, and general contractors, most often smaller teams where the owner or office still handles a lot directly.</p></details><details><summary><h3>What powers the technical side of this?</h3></summary><p>A dedicated delivery platform runs behind the scenes to handle scheduling, messaging, and follow-up. It stays out of your way. You work with Top Shelf, not a piece of software.</p></details><details><summary><h3>Is Agency OS software?</h3></summary><p>No. It is Top Shelf&#8217;s internal playbook for how work gets done. It is not sold or accessed separately.</p></details><details><summary><h3>What information is needed to begin?</h3></summary><p>Just your business details and a short description of where things currently stand. No passwords or customer data.</p></details></div></div></section>'''+cta()
write('index.html','Contractor Lead Follow-Up in North Jersey | Top Shelf Agency','Top Shelf helps North Jersey plumbers and electricians capture missed opportunities, follow up faster, earn legitimate reviews, and organize leads.',home)
package=ph('Top Shelf Contractor Growth Package','One connected system for the moments where good jobs get lost.','Built for small North Jersey plumbing and electrical companies that need a dependable customer journey.')+f'<section><div class="wrap"><div class="grid four">{cards("h2")}</div><div class="prose"><h2>Capabilities support the outcome</h2><p>Depending on what the audit confirms, the package may use missed-call text-back, forms, booking, follow-up, review requests, pipeline management, and reporting inside GoHighLevel. These are components—not separate products.</p><h2>We work with what is working</h2><p>This may already be handled internally. Nothing goes live before testing and owner approval.</p><h2>No invented promise</h2><p>Scope and timing depend on needs, access, integrations, compliance review, and testing. Pricing is not published until finalized.</p></div></div></section>'+cta();write('growth-package/index.html','Contractor Growth Package | Top Shelf Agency','A practical contractor system for missed opportunities, follow-up, reviews, and organized leads.',package,data('Service',{'serviceType':'Top Shelf Contractor Growth Package'}))
